---
import { demos } from "../data/site";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/")
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
const first = demos[0];
---

<figure class="fig grid" data-demo data-base={base}>
  <figcaption class="fig-caption">
    <span class="label"><b>Fig. 1</b></span>
    <p>π<sub>0.5</sub> on LIBERO-10 writes a one-line memory of task progress at every replan. The isolated baseline pauses the arm until each memory is finished; OxyGen keeps the arm moving and completes memories over the next frames.</p>
    <p>One RTX 4090. Model time is measured; simulation runs at the 20 Hz control rate; playback is 1×. OxyGen decodes <i>k</i> = 1 token per request per frame.</p>
  </figcaption>
  <div class="fig-body">
    <div class="demo-video">
      <video
        controls
        muted
        playsinline
        preload="metadata"
        poster={`${base}posters/${first.id}.webp`}
        data-demo-video
        aria-label={`${first.title}: OxyGen and the isolated baseline side by side`}
      >
        <source src={`${base}videos/${first.id}.mp4`} type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
    </div>
    <div class="demo-list" role="tablist" aria-label="Demo tasks">
      {demos.map((demo, index) => (
        <button
          role="tab"
          type="button"
          aria-selected={index === 0 ? "true" : "false"}
          data-id={demo.id}
          data-label={demo.title}
          title={demo.task}
        >
          <span>{demo.title}</span>
          <small>{demo.oxygenS.toFixed(1)} s vs {demo.baselineS.toFixed(1)} s · <b>{(demo.baselineS / demo.oxygenS).toFixed(2)}× sooner</b></small>
        </button>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</figure>
